{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794554244,"nonce":"20J+g5TVMhc02pxFiEIryiydMIM=","title":"Visual and layout animations still force a full paint every frame","message":"What runs today. cn expand and collapse (collapsible, accordion), the sidebar, tree view, tabs, the toast tray and the overlay stack animate through animate_bounds (a visual animation: a per-node offset, size delta and clip, read through get_render_bounds) or animate_layout (collapsing constraints applied inside compute_layout). Both are stepped on the CPU in the layout pass. While either runs, the window's present step (bounds_anim_active), the compositor (needs_walker, other_animations_active) and layout_due_since keep the frame on the full walk and a full layout.\n\nFLIP (flip.rs, 1379b4f) is a different system. It covers CSS `transition: transform` on elements a reflow moves, which in cn is mainly the reorderable-tabs neighbour slide, and it rides on rows since 241a0233. It does not reach any of the cases above, so most of the animation cost in cn is still a full paint.\n\nWhat a row can carry: the offset of a node and of what moves with it (the siblings below an expanding panel) as a translate row; a reveal or collapse clip as a clip row (the node table moves clips, 9c959d7c); opacity. What it cannot: a size delta (the node's own box growing, content reflowing inside it), and animate_layout, which changes taffy's constraints each frame so the layout is the animation.\n\nTo do:\n- Measure before building. animation_paths has no visual or layout animation scene. Add one each for a collapsible, a sidebar width and a tree expand, painted in full and by rows, and note which cn paths the demos actually hit.\n- Visual animations: split each config into the offset (a row), the clip (a row) and the size. Decide whether an expanding node's size can be a scale of a paint at the settled size, or needs its own subtree repainted over the cached layer (region replay).\n- Layout animations: lay out once at the end state and animate by translate and clip where the content does not reflow; where it must reflow, keep the layout per frame but do not repaint the rest of the tree.\n- iOS and Android are in the mobile paint issue.\n\nRelated: 1379b4f, 122c606, a0a05a2, dabc8a7, 5092663.","files":null}]}